hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1486","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, he said: Al-Alaa told us that: He entered upon Anas bin Malik in his house in Basra when he left from Dhuhr, he said: He turned it next to the mosque, so when we entered it, he said: Did you pray the afternoon prayer? We said: No, we had just finished the noon hour. He said: They prayed the afternoon prayer. He said: So we stood up and prayed. When we departed, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “That is the prayer of the hypocrite. He sat and watched the afternoon prayer until it was between the horns of Satan. He stood up and clicked.” Four, in which God is not mentioned except a little.”"
"1487","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The one who misses the afternoon prayer, it is as if he has left his family and his wealth behind.”"
"1488","Abba Ahmad bin Suleiman, he said: Abu Dawud, meaning Omar bin Saad, told us on the authority of Badr bin Uthman, he said: He dictated it to me, he said: Abu Dawud told us Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, said: A beggar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him about the times for prayer, but he did not answer him anything. So he ordered Bilal to perform the iqamaat at dawn when it broke, then he ordered him to perform the iqamaat for the noon prayer when the sun had set, and the one who said it said: The middle of the day or And He knows best: Then he ordered him to perform the iqama in the afternoon prayer while the sun was high. Then he ordered him to perform the iqamaat in the sunset prayer when the sun had set, then he ordered him to, So he stayed for the evening prayer when twilight had set, then he delayed dawn the next day until he left. The one who said it said: The sun rose or, then he delayed noon until It was close to the time of the afternoon prayer yesterday, then he delayed the afternoon prayer and then left, and the one who said it said: The sun turned red or, then he delayed the sunset until it was When twilight fell, then he delayed dinner until a third of the night, and said: “The time is between these two.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1489","Abba Amr bin Ali, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Azdi speaking, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, Shu’bah said: Qatada would raise it sometimes, and sometimes he would not raise it. He said: “The time for the noon prayer unless The afternoon prayer arrives, and the time for the afternoon prayer is as long as the sun has not yet set, and the time for the sunset prayer is as long as the twilight twilight does not fall, and the time for the evening prayer is unless The middle of the night comes, and it is morning unless the sun rises.”"
"1490","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs a rak’ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, or a rak’ah of the afternoon prayer In the morning, before the sun had risen, he had arrived.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1491","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Araj, They narrate to him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs a rak’ah of the morning prayer before it begins \"" 1492"""""
"1492","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la informed us, saying: Al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Whoever catches a rak'ah of the 'Asr prayer before the sun sets, or a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, has caught (the prayer)."""""
"1493","Anba Amr bin Mansour said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If one of you performs the first prostration of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, let him complete his prayer. If he performs the first prostration of the morning prayer before the sun rises, then he should complete his prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1494","Abba Amr bin Ali, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Hassan, he said: Al-Hajjaj came and we asked Jabir bin Abdullah, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the noon and afternoon prayers, And the sun is pure white, and it is sunset when the sun sets, and it is evening; sometimes, when he sees them gathered, he hastens, and when He saw that they had slowed down again.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1495","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told me, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith told us, Thawr said: Sulayman bin Musa told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the times of prayer, and he said: “Pray with me,” so he prayed the noon prayer when it deviated. The sun, and the afternoon when the shade of everything was as it was, and the sunset when the sun had set, and the evening prayer when the twilight had set. He said: “Then he prayed the noon prayer when “The man’s condition was the same as that of man, and the afternoon was when the man’s condition was twice that of it, and the Maghrib was when it was before the twilight twilight,” said Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith: He said in the evening: I watch until a third of the night."
"1496","Anba Yusuf bin Wadhid said: Qudamah, meaning Ibn Shihab, told us on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: That Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to teach him the times for prayer, so Gabriel came forward, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, followed him. The people were behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he prayed the noon prayer when the sun had passed the zenith, and he came to him when the man’s shadow was like his person, and he did as He did so, and Gabriel came forward, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, followed him, and the people behind the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he prayed the afternoon prayer. Then he came to it when the sun had set, and Gabriel came forward, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was behind him, and the people were behind the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him and prayed the sunset prayer, then he came to it when twilight had disappeared, and Gabriel came forward, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed him, and the people were behind him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he prayed the evening prayer, then he came to him when dawn broke, and Gabriel and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward. He succeeded him, and the people followed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he prayed the morning prayer, then he came to him on the second day when the man’s shadow was like his person. So he did what he had done yesterday, so he prayed the noon prayer, then he came to him when the man’s shadow was like his two figures, so he did what he had done yesterday, so he prayed the afternoon prayer. Then he came to him when the sun had set, and he did as he had done yesterday, so he prayed the Maghrib prayer, and we slept, then we got up, then we slept, then we got up, so he came to him. So he did what he had done yesterday, so he prayed the evening prayer, then he said: “There is a time between these two prayers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1497","Suwaid bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali bin Hussein, he said: Wahb bin Kaysan told me, he said: Jabir told us Ibn Abdullah, he said: “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sun was setting, and he said: Get up, O Muhammad, and he prayed the noon prayer when it was setting. The sun, then he stayed until the man’s face was like that. He came to him to pray the afternoon prayer and said: Get up, O Muhammad. So he prayed the afternoon prayer, then he stayed until the afternoon prayer. The sun had set, and he came to him and said: Get up and pray the Maghrib prayer. So he stood up and prayed it when the sun had set at the same time, then he stayed until when twilight had set, he came to him. So he said: Get up and pray the evening prayer, so he got up and prayed it, then he came to him when dawn was shining, and he said: Get up, O Muhammad, and pray, so he got up and prayed. In the morning, then he came to him the next day when the man’s veil was like that, and he said: Get up, O Muhammad, and pray. So he prayed the noon prayer, then he came to him when the man’s veil was Double it, and he said: Get up, O Muhammad. So he prayed the afternoon prayer, then he came to the sunset when the sun had set for a single time, and he did not stop there, so he said: Get up. He prayed, so he prayed Maghrib, then he came to him for the evening prayer when the first third of the night had passed, and he said: Get up. He prayed, so he prayed the evening prayer, then he came to him. In the morning, when he had arrived very early, he said: “Get up and pray.” So he prayed the morning prayer, then he said: “There is a whole amount of time between these two.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1498","Narrated by Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Sadaqa, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He prays the evening prayer when twilight disappears.”"
"1499","Anba Muhammad ibn Qudamah said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Raqbah, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Habib ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Bashir. He said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the times for this prayer, the evening of the afterlife. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray it for the third time before the moon had fallen. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1500","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Affan told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Bashir bin Thabit, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: “By God, I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time for this prayer, the last night’s prayer. The Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prays it for a third time after the moon sets.”"
"1501","Anba Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Awf, who is Ibn Abi Jamila, on the authority of Sayyar bin Salamah Abi Al-Minhal, he said: I entered And my father went to Abu Barza Al-Aslami, and my father said to him, “Tell us how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the obligatory prayer?” He said: “He used to pray the afternoon prayer,” until he said: “And he liked to delay the evening prayer, which you call the ‘Umma prayer.” He said: “And he disliked it.” Sleeping before it, and the conversation after it is brief."
"1502","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “This is Gabriel, who came to you to teach you your religion. He prayed for him the evening prayer when the twilight of the night had passed, then he came to him the next day and he prayed. Then he prayed the evening prayer, briefly. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1503","Amr ibn Hisham told me, he said: Mukhlid ibn Yazid al-Harrani told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the time for prayer, and he said: “Stand up.” “We have these two days with us.” So he ordered Bilal to stand at dawn and pray the dawn prayer, then he ordered him to pray the noon prayer when the sun had passed. He commanded him when he saw that the sun was white, so he stayed for the afternoon prayer, then he commanded him when the veil of the sun had fallen, so he stayed for the sunset prayer, then he commanded him when twilight had set, so he stayed at sunset. for the evening prayer, then he commanded him the next day, so he lit it at dawn, then it cooled down at noon, so he was blessed to let it cool down, then he prayed the afternoon prayer, and the sun White, and he delayed that, then he prayed the Maghrib prayer before twilight had set, then he ordered him, so he stayed for dinner when a third of the night had passed, So he prayed it, then he said: “Where is the one who asked about the time for prayer? The time for your prayer is between what you saw.”"
"1504","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Ibn Himyar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Abla told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a dark night, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, called out to him: The women and children slept. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: “No one is waiting for it except you.” And it was not being prayed at that time except in Medina. Then he said: “Pray.” “Between the disappearance of twilight and a third of the night.”"
"1505","And the wording is from Ibn Himyar. Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Al-Mughirah bin told me. Hakim, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Abu Bakr, that she told him, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night Until the rest of the people of the night had departed, and until the people of the mosque slept, then he went out and prayed, then he said: “It is its time, had it not been too difficult for my nation.”"
"1506","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Sayyar bin Salamah told us, he said: I heard my father, Abu Barza Al-Aslami asked about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: Did you hear it? He said: Just as I hear you now. He said: I heard my father asking him about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “He was indifferent to some Delaying it. He said: This means dinner until midnight, and he does not like sleeping before it or talking after it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1507","Anba Ali bin Hajar said: Ismail told us, he said: Humaid told us, he said: Anas was asked: Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wear a ring? He said: Yes, he delayed the last night of the evening prayer until half the night. When he had prayed, he turned to us with his face and said: “You will not stop praying.” “In a prayer that you have not waited for,” Anas said: “It is as if I am looking at the gleam of his seal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1508","Abba Imran bin Musa, he said: Abd Al-Warith told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: He prayed with us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Maghrib prayer, then he did not go out to us until half of the night had passed, so he went out and prayed with them, then he said: “The people have prayed and slept, and you are still in prayer as long as you wait for the prayer. Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the sickness of the sick, I would have commanded this prayer to be delayed until midnight.”"
"1509","Abba Utbah bin Abdullah said: I read to Malik bin Anas, and Al-Harith bin Miskin read to him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If only people knew what is in The call, and the first row, then they had no choice but to push towards it. They would have pressed, and if they had known what was in the migration, they would have raced to it, even if They know what is in the darkness, and the morning will come to them, even if they crawl.”"
"1510","Anba Ahmad bin Suleiman said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you regarding this name of your prayer, for they obscure the Camels, and that is the evening meal.”"
"1511","Anba Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, reported, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salama. Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the pulpit: “Do not let the Bedouins defeat you because of the name “Your prayer is not the evening prayer.”"
"1512","Anba Muhammad bin Bashar told us: Yahya told us, he said: Awf told us, he said: Sayyar bin Salamah told me, he said: I entered upon Abu Barza, My father asked him: How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray the obligatory prayer? He said: “He used to pray the afternoon prayer, which you call the first, when the sun is setting, and he used to pray the afternoon prayer when one of us returned to his journey at the farthest part of the city.” And the sun is alive, and I forgot what he said about Morocco, and he liked to delay the evening meal, which you call darkness, and he hated sleeping. Before that, and the hadith after it, and he used to leave the morning prayer when the man recognized his companion, and he used to recite from sixty to one hundred.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1513","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein told us, on the authority of His father, that Jabir bin Abdullah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the dawn prayer when it became clear to him that it was dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1514","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him About the time for the morning prayer, and when we arrived the next morning, he ordered, when dawn had broken, that the prayer should be performed, so he led us in prayer, and when it was the next morning, he departed, then He ordered, and the prayer was established, so he led us in prayer, then he said: “Where is the one who asked about the time for prayer? What time is there between these two?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1515","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were They pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning, wrapped in their cloaks, and then they return, and no one recognizes them from the deceit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1516","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “peace be upon him, to perform the Fajr prayer, and the women would leave, covering themselves with their cloaks, and not knowing that they had been undressed.”"
"1517","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sulaiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He prayed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Khaybar in Ghalas, while he was close to them, attacked them and said: “God is great, Khaybar has been destroyed. “When we camped in a people’s place, the morning of those who had been warned would be bad.”"
"1518","Abba Ubaid Allah bin Saeed said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told me, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid. On the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Travel at dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1519","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Abu Ghassan told us, he said: Zaid bin Aslam told me, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of men from his people from the Ansar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Travel in the morning, for that is the greatest reward.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1520","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Sadaqa, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He prays the afterlife of Isha’ when twilight disappears, then he said after that: He does not pray Fajr until the sight is clear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1521","Muhammad bin Rafi’ reported, saying: Zakaria bin Adi told us, saying: Ibn Al-Mubarak reported, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever performs a rak’ah of dawn before the sun rises, has performed it. And whoever performs a rak’ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, he has performed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1522","Anba Imran bin Musa said: Muhammad bin Sawa told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs one rak’ah of the morning prayer before the first horn of the sun rises, has performed, And whoever performs one or two rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, he has performed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1523","Narrated by Ibrahim bin Muhammad and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, and the pronunciation for him, he said: Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, he said: He narrated to me Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever performs a prostration in the morning before it rises... “The sun has reached it, and whoever performs the afternoon prostration before the sun sets, he has reached it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1524","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdullah bin Idris reported, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Umar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever catches up with a rak’ah of prayer has done it.”"
"1525","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever performs one rak’ah of prayer has completed the prayer.”"
"1526","Yazid bin Muhammad bin Abdul Samad told me, he said: Hisham Al-Attar told us, he said: Ismail, who is the son of Abdullah bin Sama’ah, on the authority of Musa bin Ayan, on the authority of Abu Amr, meaning Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever performs one rak’ah of prayer has completed the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1527","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever catches up with a rak’ah of prayer has done it,” Abu Abd al-Rahman: We do not know of anyone who followed Abu al-Mughirah on what he said: On the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and the correct one is on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah"
"1528","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar, and Musa bin Sulaiman bin Ismail bin Al-Qasim, and the wording for it, told me: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Who has realized one rak’ah of Friday prayer or any other rak’ah, and his prayer has been completed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1529","Abba Muhammad bin Ismail said: Ayoub bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs a rak’ah of one of the prayers, has performed it, unless He makes up for what he missed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1530","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdullah al-Sanabihi, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The sun is rising, and with it is the horn of Satan. When it rises, separate it. When it sets, compare it. So when it has passed, separate it. When it approaches sunset, compare it. When it sets, separate it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. “about praying in those hours.”"
"1531","Anba Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Musa bin Ali bin Rabah, he said: I heard my father, saying: I heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani. He says: For three hours, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from praying during them, or burying our dead in them: when the sun rose. “When the sun rises until it rises, and when the noonday star rises until it sets, and when the sun sets until it sets.”"
"1532","Anba Amr bin Mansour told us: Adam told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: Abu told me Yahya Sulaym bin Amir, Damra bin Habib, and Abu Talha Nu`aym bin Ziyad said: We heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili say: I heard Amr bin Absa says: I said: O Messenger of God, is there one hour closer than the other? Or is it an hour that it is safe to mention? He said: “Yes, the closest a servant will be to the Lord is in the middle of the night. If you are able to be among those who remember God in that hour, then be.” Prayer is witnessed and attended until the rising of the sun, for it rises between the horns of Satan, and it is the hour for the disbelievers to pray, so abandon prayer until The chain of a spear will rise, and its rays will go away, then prayer will be attended and witnessed, until the sun is at the same level as the spear at midday. For it is an hour when the gates of Hell will be opened and it will be set in smoke, so abandon prayer until the fay is finished, then prayer will be attended and witnessed until the sun sets. For it disappears between the horns of Satan, and it is the hour of prayer of the disbelievers.”"
"1533","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun had set, and prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun had risen. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1534","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: “The The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade praying at sunrise or sunset.”"
"1535","Abba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak said: Al-Fadl bin Anbasa, trustworthy, narrated to us, saying: Wahib reported, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father He said: Aisha said: Ibn Umar was delusional: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, only forbade one to ascertain whether the sun would rise or set. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1536","Anba Humayd bin Masada said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Uqba bin Amir, saying: “Three There are hours during which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from praying or burying our dead in them: when the sun rose until It rises, and when the afternoon rises until it sets, and when it adds to the sunset until it sets.”"
"1537","Abba Mujahid bin Musa said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Damra bin Saeed, he heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, about prayer after dawn until sunrise, and about prayer after afternoon until sunset."
"1538","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, he said: my father told me, he said: he told me Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the sun’s visor rises, delay the prayer until it rises. If the sun’s visor sets, So delay the prayer until sunset.”"
"1539","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: my father told me, he said: Ibn Omar told me, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not focus your prayer on the rising or setting of the sun, for it rises between the horns of Satan. And you set down between the horns of Satan.”"
"1540","I am Amr bin Ali. He said: Abd al-Rahman told us. He said: Shu’bah and Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Wahb. Ibn Al-Ajja', on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray after the afternoon prayer, unless you pray while the sun is high.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1541","Anba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, he said: Aisha said: “What the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left behind.” May God bless him and grant him peace, I have never performed the two prostrations after the afternoon prayer.”"
"1542","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mugheerah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Aisha said: He did not enter upon me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the afternoon prayer, except for their two prayers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1543","Anba Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, said: I heard Masruq and Al-Aswad, saying: We bear witness to Aisha, that she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to: If he was with me after the afternoon prayer, they would pray.”"
"1544","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Harmala, told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that he asked Aisha, Concerning the two rak’ahs that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray after the afternoon prayer, she said: He used to pray them before the afternoon prayer, So he was distracted from them or forgot about them, so he prayed them after the afternoon prayer, and whenever he prayed a prayer he would continue it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1545","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Al-Mu`tamir, said: I heard Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: “He prayed two rak’ahs at once in her house after the afternoon prayer,” and that she mentioned that to him, so he said: “They are two rak’ahs that I performed.” I prayed them after noon, so I was distracted by them until I prayed the afternoon prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1546","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Talha bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was distracted from the two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer, so he prayed them after the afternoon prayer.”"
"1547","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr told us, He said: I later asked about the two rak’ahs at sunset, and he said: Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr was praying them, so Muawiyah sent to him: What are these two? The two rak'ahs at sunset? The hadith was forced to go to Umm Salamah, and Umm Salamah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer. So he distracted them, so he kneeled on them when the sun had set, and I did not see him praying them before or after.”"
"1548","Abba Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Muhammad, he said: I heard Nafi`, narrating on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hafsa, that she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would only pray when dawn came.” “Two light rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1549","Ayoub bin Muhammad told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Yazid bin Talq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Bilamani, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, who Did he convert to Islam with you? He said: A free man and a slave. He said: I said: Is there any hour closer to God than another? He said: Yes, the middle of the last night, so pray whatever seems to you. Until you pray Fajr, then finish until the sun rises, as long as it is like a sheet of paper until it spreads, then pray as long as you like until the pillar rises. On his shade, then stop until the sun has passed, for Hell is dark during the middle of the day, then pray as long as you like until you pray the afternoon prayer, then stop until “When the sun sets, it sets between the horns of Satan, and rises between the horns of Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1550","Abba Muhammad bin Mansour said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard from Abu Al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Babah, speaking on the authority of Jubayr. Bin Mutim, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying at any time he wants.” \Night or day\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1551","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. If he departed before the sun had set, he would delay the prayer until the time of the afternoon prayer, then he would come down and combine them. If the sun had set, Before setting off, he prayed the noon prayer, then rode.”"
"1552","Anba Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported on the authority of him, and the pronunciation is his, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl Aamir ibn Wathilah, that Muadh ibn Jabal told him that they went out with the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the year of Tabuk. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to combine the noon, afternoon, and sunset times. And the evening prayer, so he delayed the prayer for a day, then he went out and prayed the noon and afternoon prayers all together, then he entered, then he went out and prayed the sunset and evening prayers. \Everyone\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1553","Anba Abu Asim Khushish ibn Asram said: Hibban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd. On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He combined the first prayer with Basra, and the afternoon prayer, and there is nothing between them, and the sunset prayer, and the evening prayer, and there is nothing between them. This is out of occupancy, and Ibn Abbas claimed that he prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the first city of Medina, and the afternoon prayer was eight prostrations that were not \There is something between them.\"""""""
"1554","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Jabir bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that: “If he was in a hurry to travel, he would delay the noon prayer until the time of Asr, so he combines them, and delays Maghrib until he combines them, and Isha’ when twilight disappears.”"
"1555","Abba Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If travel hastened him, he should delay the Maghrib prayer until he combined it with the evening prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1556","I am Qutaybah bin Saeed. He said: Al-Attaf bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: We came with Ibn Umar from Mecca until that time. Tonight, he walked until evening, when we thought he had forgotten to pray, so we told him: “Prayer,” so he remained silent, and walked until twilight was almost gone, then he descended. So he prayed, and twilight disappeared, so he prayed the evening prayer, then he came to us and said: “This is what we used to do with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the time came. walk in it\"" 1557"""""
"1557","Mahmud ibn Khalid informed me, saying: Al-Walid — meaning ibn Muslim — narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jabir narrated to us, saying: Nafi' narrated to me, saying: I went out with 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar on a journey to a land of his. A man came to him saying: ""Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd is in such-and-such condition, and we do not think she will survive."" He hurried out, accompanied by a Qurashi man. The sun set, yet he did not shorten the prayer — and I knew him to be one who guarded the prayer. When he delayed, I said: ""The prayer, may Allah have mercy on you."" He turned to me and continued until the last of the twilight. Then he dismounted, prayed Maghrib, then established 'Isha' after the twilight had disappeared, and prayed with us. Then he turned to us and said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when travel pressed him, would do like this."""""
"1558","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman, a sheikh from Quraysh, who said: “ I accompanied Ibn Umar to the fever, and when the sun set, I rushed to tell him prayer, so he walked until the white of the horizon was gone, and the charcoal of dinner was gone. He prayed Maghrib three rak'ahs, then prayed two rak'ahs after that, then he said: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing."
"1559","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abu Usama reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Ali bin Abu Talib, he used to walk when the sun had set, and even when it was almost dark, he would come down and pray the Maghrib prayer, then he would say his evening prayer. So he eats, then prays the evening prayer after that, then he says: “This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1560","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was going hard, He combined Maghrib and Isha'"
"1561","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Peace and blessings of God be upon him, the noon and afternoon prayers all together, and the sunset and evening prayers all together, without fear or travel.”"
"1562","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz reported, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa Abu Abdullah reported, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray in Medina, combining the two prayers: noon and afternoon. And Maghrib and Isha' without fear or rain. It was said to him: Why? He said: “So that there will be no hardship upon his nation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1563","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, he said: We entered on Jabir bin Abdullah, so I said, “Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked until he came to Arafat, and he camped there, until when the sun had set, he ordered the people to perform the ritual prayer, and it departed.” Until he reached the bottom of the valley, he addressed the people, then Bilal called the call to prayer, then he stayed and prayed the noon prayer, then he stayed and prayed the afternoon prayer, but he did not pray. \nothing between them\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1564","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari told him that: “He prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the farewell Hajj, the Maghrib and evening prayers at Muzdalifah all together.” \"" 1565"""""
"1565","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim informed us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: I was with Ibn 'Umar when he departed from 'Arafat. When he came to Muzdalifah, he combined Maghrib and 'Isha. When he finished, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did in this place the like of what I did."""""
"1566","Abba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, he is Ibn Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abd God said: “I have never seen the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combining two prayers except by combining them, and he prayed the morning prayer that day before its time.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1567","Anba Al-Hussein bin Harith said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was returning from Arafat. When he came to the people, he came down and urinated. He did not say: He spilled water. He said: So I poured water on him. So he performed a light ablution, and I said: The prayer. He said: “The prayer is before you.” When he came to Muzdalifah, he prayed the Maghrib prayer, then they took off the prayer. their journey, then he prayed the evening prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1568","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Al-Eizar told me, he said: I heard Abu Amr Al-Shaybani said: The owner of this house told us, and he pointed to the house of Abdullah, and said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which Is work more beloved to God? He said: “Prayer at its appointed time, honoring one’s parents, and jihad in the path of God.”"
"1569","Anba Yahya bin Hakim said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, that: It was In the mosque of Omar bin Shurahbil, the prayer was established, and they waited for him, so he came and said: I was performing Witr, and he said: Abdullah was asked: Did Is there a string after the call to prayer? He said: “Yes, and after the Iqama.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1570","It was narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that: “He fell asleep and missed prayer until the sun rose, then he prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1571","Anba Qutaybah bin Saeed, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: They mentioned Their sleep in the absence of prayer, to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding that, and he said: “There is no negligence in sleep, but rather negligence in wakefulness, so if “If one of you forgets to pray or falls asleep, let him pray it when he remembers it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1572","Suwaid bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no negligence in sleeping, but negligence is imposed on one who does not pray the prayer.” Until the time for the next prayer comes, so that he pays attention to it.”"
"1573","Anba Amr bin Ali told us: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell asleep and missed the prayer until the sun rose, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let him pray it.” “One of you from tomorrow until its time.”"
"1574","Anba Humayd ibn Masada, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, said: Hajjaj al-Ahwal told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a man who neglects to pray or neglects it. He said: “The expiation for it is that he prays it when he remembers it.” \"" 1575"""""
"1575","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it."""""
"1576","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of his father, who said: “We were with the Messenger of God He, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, so we took him captive for the night, and when the dawn came, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came down and he slept and the people slept. With him, we did not wake up until the sun had risen over us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the muezzin, and he gave the call to prayer, then he prayed the two rak’ahs. Before dawn, then he commanded him, so he stood and led the people in prayer, then he informed us of what was going to happen until the Hour came.”"
"1577","I am Ya’qub bin Ibrahim. He said: Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan. He said: Abu Hazim told me, on the authority of my father. Hurairah, he said: We had a wedding with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we did not wake up until the sun rose, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Each man takes the head of his camel, for this is a place where Satan came to us. He said: So we did so. He called for water, and he performed ablution, then He prostrated two prostrations, then the prayer was established, and he prayed the morning prayer.”"
"1578","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Nafi` ibn Jubayr ibn Mut`im, on the authority of Abu Ubaida bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were detained from the noon prayer. And the afternoon, and the sunset, and the evening, and that became difficult for me, so I said: We are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the path of God, So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered: Bilal, so he stayed and led the noon prayer with us, then he stayed and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he stayed and prayed the sunset prayer. Then he stayed and prayed the evening prayer, then he came around us and said: “There is not a group on earth who remember Allah except you.”"
"1579","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya, the judge of Damascus, and Ibrahim bin Al-Hassan Al-Masisi informed me, saying: Hajjaj told us, he said Ibn Jurayj said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, that: He used to say: When the Muslims came to Medina, they would gather. So they used to perform the prayers, but no one called for them. One day they spoke about that, and some of them said: Make a bell like the Christian bell, and he said: Some of them said: Rather, a century like the century of the Jews. Omar said: Will you not send a man to call to prayer? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Bilal, get up and call for prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1580","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “He ordered Bilal to recite the call to prayer and to pronounce the Iqamat Witr.”"
"1581","Abba Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Ja`far told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: “During the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the call to prayer was given two times, and the iqamah was given once, except that you say: The prayer has begun, it has begun.” \Prayer\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1582","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdul-Wahid, he said: Makhoul told us, on the authority of Abdul Allah bin Muhayriz, on the authority of Abu Mahdhurah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He taught him the call to prayer nineteen words, and the Iqamah seven words.” Ten words, then Abu Mahdhurah counted them as nineteen, and seventeen.”"
"1583","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Muadh bin Hisham reported, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Amir Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhairiz, on the authority of Abu Mahdhurah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me the call to prayer, and he said: “God is great, God is great, God is great.” I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad Messenger of God, then he returns and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness Indeed, Muhammad is the Messenger of God, hail the prayer, hail the prayer, hail the success, hail the success, God is great, God is the greatest, there is no god but God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1584","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan and Yusuf bin Saeed told me, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Hajjaj told me, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Abdul told me Al-Aziz bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Mahdhura, that Abdullah bin Muhairiz told him that he was an orphan in Ubai’s lap. Mahdhura Until he prepared him for the Levant, he said: I said to my father with caution: Yes, uncle, I am going to the Levant, and I fear that I will be asked about your harm, so he informed me. Abu Mahdhoora said to him: Yes, I went out with a group, and we were on the road to Hunayn, which was closed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Hunayn. We met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some road, and the muezzin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, announced the call to prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so we heard the voice of the muezzin, while we were facing him, so we kept telling him and mocking him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard him. The voice, peace be upon him, was sent to us until we stood before him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Which of you whose voice I heard has He rose.” The people pointed to me, and they spoke the truth, so he sent them all out and detained me, and said: “Stand up and announce the call to prayer.” So I stood up, and he turned to me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Adhan himself, said: Say: “God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then he said: Go back, extend your voice, then say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, hail the prayer, hail the prayer, hail the success, hail the success, God is great, God is the greatest, there is no god Except Allah.” Then he called me when I had finished the call to prayer, and he gave me a bag containing some silver, so I said: O Messenger of God, tell me to call the call to prayer in Mecca. He said: “I have ordered you to do so.” So I went to Attab ibn Usayd, the employee of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, and I announced the call to prayer with him on behalf of The command of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1585","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: My father and Umm Abd told me. Al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhura, on the authority of Abi Mahdhura, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out from Hunayn, I went out to meet ten people. We were looking for them from the people of Mecca. We heard them calling to prayer, so we stood up and made the call to prayer, mocking them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “I heard in these people the call to prayer of a man with a good voice, so he sent for us, and we called the call to prayer, man by man, and I was the last of them. He said when I gave the call to prayer:” Come.” So he made me sit in front of him, and he wiped my forelock and blessed me three times, then he said: “Go and give the call to prayer at the Sacred House,” I said. How, O Messenger of God? So he taught me what they call the call to prayer now: “God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, I bear witness that there is no god. Except Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, Hail to prayer, Hail to prayer, Hail to Al-Falah, hail to Al-Falah, prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep, in the first day of the morning, God is great, God is great, there is no god but God He said: He taught me the Iqama twice: “God is the greatest, God is the greatest, God is the greatest, God is the greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness There is no god but God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, hail the prayer, hail the prayer, hail the farmer, Hail to the farmer, God is great, God is great, there is no god but God.” Ibn Juraij said: Uthman told me this whole news, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Umm Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhura, that they heard that from Abi Mahdhura. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1586","Hajib bin Sulaiman told me, on the authority of Waki`, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Malik bin al-Huwayrith, he said: I and a cousin of mine came, and he once said to me and a companion of mine, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “When you travel, give us the call to prayer, and stay, and let them lead you in prayer.” \the eldest of you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1587","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwayrith, he said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were young people close together, so we stayed with him for twenty nights. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May God bless him and grant him peace, Merciful and Compassionate. He thought that we missed our families, and he asked us about those of our families who had left us, so we told him. He said: “Go back to your families, stay with them, teach them, and pass them by. When the time for prayer comes, let one of you call the call to prayer and lead you in prayer.” \The eldest of you\"""""""
"1588","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Amr bin Salamah. Abu Qalaba said to me: He is alive. Have you not met him? Ayoub said: I met him and asked him, and he said: When the conquest took place, every nation hastened to convert to Islam, so my father went to convert to Islam. The family of Eve, and when he came, we received him, and he said: I have come to you, by God, truly from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Pray Pray such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time, and pray such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time. When the time for prayer comes, let one of you call the call to prayer, and let most of you lead in prayer. Quran"
"1589","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Bilāla gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls.”"
"1590","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bilala gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until you hear the admonition of Ibn Umm Maktum.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1591","Abba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “When Bilal gives the call to prayer, then eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer.” She said: There was nothing between them until this was revealed. And this goes up"
"1592","Abba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hushaym, said: Mansour informed us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his aunt, Anisa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer, then eat and drink, and when Bilal gives the call to prayer, do not eat, nor do \Drink\"""""""
"1593","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Al-Mu`tamir bin Suleiman reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, to wake you up who is sleeping, and for your leader to return, and not to say it like this, meaning in the morning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1594","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Yazid, who is the son of Harun, reported, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, that a questioner, he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace peace be upon him, about the time of dawn, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered: “Bilal, so he called the call to prayer when dawn came, and when it was the next day, he delayed it.” dawn until dawn, then he commanded him, so he stood and prayed, then he said: This is the time for prayer.”"
"1595","Anba Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfa, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, so Bilal came out and called the call to prayer, and he started saying: “In his call to prayer this is how he swerved to the right and to the left.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1596","Anba Muhammad bin Salamah said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin told me. Abu Sa`sa`ah al-Ansari and then al-Mazini, on the authority of his father, that: He told him that Abu Sa`id al-Khudri said to him: “I see you love sheep.” And the desert. If you are among your sheep or desert, and you announce the call to prayer, raise your voice, for the voice of the muezzin is not heard by a jinn. “And there is not a human being, nor a thing, but that it will bear witness to him on the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Sa’id said: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1597","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Yazid told us, he is Ibn Zuray’. He said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Abu Yahya, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he heard it from the mouth of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The muezzin will be forgiven for extending his voice, and every utterance will bear witness to him. \and dry\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1598","Abba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Kufi, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Single, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God and His angels pray in the front row, and the muezzin is forgiven for extending his voice.” And whoever hears it believes it whether it is wet or dry, and he will have a reward similar to whoever prays with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1599","I am Suwaid bin Nasr. He said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Salman, on the authority of Abu Mahdhurah. He said: “I used to give the call to prayer. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I used to say in the first dawn call to prayer: Hail to prayer, hail to success, prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than “Sleep, God is great, God is great, there is no god but God.” Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Yahya and Abd al-Rahman told us, saying: He told us Sufyan, with this chain of transmission and similar to it, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi said: Abu Ja`far al-Farra is not (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1600","Anba Muhammad bin Ma’dan bin Isa Al-Harrani said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Bilal, said: “The last call to prayer is God is great, God is great, there is no god but God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1601","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: “It was the last call to prayer of Bilal.” “God is great, God is great, there is no god but God,” Anba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, About black: like that"
"1602","Suwaid bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, he said: Al-Aswad bin Yazid told me, On the authority of Abu Mahdhurah, he narrated: “The last call to prayer is: There is no god but Allah.”"
"1603","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, he said: A man from Thaqif told me: “He heard The caller of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning on a rainy night while traveling, saying: “Come to prayer, come to success, pray on your journeys.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1604","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar called for prayer on a cold, windy night, and he said: Don’t they pray while traveling? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order the muezzin, when it was a cold, rainy night, to say: “Don’t pray while traveling.”"
"1605","Anba Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi said: Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked until he came to Arafat, and he found the dome had been struck for him with a pin, so he descended with it.” Until when the sun had risen, he ordered the people to perform the prayer, and it set off for him, until when he reached the bottom of the valley, he addressed the people, then Bilal gave the call to prayer, then He stayed and prayed the noon prayer, then he stayed and prayed the afternoon prayer, and did not pray anything in between.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1606","Anba Ibrahim bin Harun told us: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, that Jabir bin Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drove until he reached Muzdalifah and prayed the Maghrib and evening prayers there with the call to prayer. And two iqamas, and he did not pray anything between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1607","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Sharik reported, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We were with him in a group and he gave the call to prayer. Then he stood up and led us in the Maghrib prayer, then he said: “The prayer.” Then he led us in the evening prayer with two rak’ahs. I said: What is this prayer? He said: “Thus.” I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1608","Anba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Salamah bin Kuhayl told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: “He prayed Maghrib and Isha’ prayers in congregation, and then he narrated on the authority of Ibn Umar that he did the same thing, and Ibn Umar narrated: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did something like that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1609","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Umar that: “He prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in congregation, with one iqama.”"
"1610","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father: That the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He brought them together at Muzdalifah, each one of them prayed standing, and he did not perform voluntary prayers before one of them, nor \After that\"""""""
"1611","Anba Amr bin Ali told us: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, said: “The polytheists occupied us on the day of the ditch, absent the noon prayer, until the sun set, and that was before the In battle, what was sent down is sent down, so God sent down: And God is sufficient for the believers in fighting, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Bilal, so he gave permission. for the noon prayer, so he prayed it at its time, then he gave the call for the afternoon prayer, so he prayed it at its time, then he gave the call for the sunset prayer, so he prayed it at its time.”"
"1612","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Abdullah said: “The The polytheists occupied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with four prayers in the ditch: so he commanded Bilal, and he called the call to prayer, then he stood, and he prayed the noon prayer, then He stayed and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he stayed and prayed the sunset prayer, then he stayed and prayed the evening prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1613","Anba Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, he said: Hisham told us, that Abu Al-Zubayr Al-Makki told them, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, that Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Masoud, He told them that Abdullah bin Masoud said: We were on a campaign, and the polytheists prevented us from praying the noon, afternoon, and sunset prayers. And dinner. When the polytheists had departed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a caller, and he stood for the noon prayer. We prayed, and he stood for the noon prayer. for the afternoon prayer, so we prayed, and he stayed for the sunset prayer, so we prayed, and he stayed for the evening prayer, so we prayed, then he came around to us, then he said: “ There is not on earth a group of people who remember Allah other than you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a strange hadith from the hadith of Sa’id, on the authority of Hisham. No one else narrated it. Excessive"
"1614","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Suwayd bin Qais narrated to him, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed one day. Then he gave the salutation while there was one rak’ah left from the prayer. Then a man caught up with him and said: I forgot a rak’ah of the prayer. So he entered the mosque and ordered Bilal. He established the prayer and prayed one rak’ah for the people. I told those people about this, and they said to me: Do you know the man? So I said: No, unless I see him. Then he passed by me, and I said: This is him. They said: He is Talha bin Ubaid Allah.”"
"1615","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abdul Rahman reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabi’ah, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard the voice of a man calling the call to prayer, so he started saying, like what he says until the message is conveyed: “I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of “Allah.” Al-Hakam said: “I did not hear this from Ibn Abi Laila.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is from a shepherd or a man.” He is celibate from his family.” Then he descended into the valley, and behold there was a shepherd of sheep, and behold there was a dead sheep, and he said: “Do you think this is easy for me?” Its people? They said: Yes. He said: “This world is easier for God than this world for its people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1616","Anba Muhammad bin Salamah said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, that Abu Ashaana Al-Maafiri told him, on the authority of Uqba bin Aamer said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Your Lord marvels at a shepherd at the top of the mountain’s ridge, calling to prayer.” And he prays, and God says: Look at this servant of mine. He calls the call to prayer and performs the prayer. He fears Me. I have forgiven my servant and admitted him to Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1617","Anba Ali bin Hajar said: Ismail told us, he said: Yahya bin Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad bin Rafi’ al-Zarqi told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in the mosque one day. Rifa’ah said: While we were with him, a man like a Bedouin came and prayed, then he shortened his prayer, then he left and greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “And upon you, go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he returned and prayed. Then he came and greeted him, and said: “And upon you.” So go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he did that two or three times, and all of that came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And you must go back, for you have not prayed.” So the people rebelled, and it became difficult for them to Someone who neglected his prayers would not have prayed, so the man said at the end of that: Show me or teach me, for I am only a human being and I make mistakes, and I make mistakes, so he said to the man “When you stand up to pray, perform ablution as God has commanded you, then recite the tashahhud, stand up, then say the takbir, and if you have a Qur’an with you, recite it. Otherwise, praise God, glorify Him, and praise God, then bow down, then be at ease while bowing, then stand upright, then prostrate, then stand upright in prostration, then Sit down, feel comfortable sitting, then stand up. If you do that, your prayer has been completed, but if you detract from it, it detracts from your prayer, and it does not \It all goes away\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1618","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad Al-Awar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Abu Jafar, the naked muezzin in the Bani Hilal Mosque, narrates, on the authority of Muslim Abi Al-Muthanna, the muezzin of the Jami’ Mosque, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that He said: During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the call to prayer was only given twice, and the iqama once, except that he says: “The prayer has begun.” “The prayer has begun.” So when we heard the iqamah, we would perform ablution, then we would go out to pray. Shu’bah said: I do not remember anything other than this from him. Hadith alone (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1619","Ali ibn Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me He, peace and blessings be upon him, and a friend of mine: “When the time for prayer comes, then announce the call to prayer, then perform the iqama, then let the eldest of you lead in prayer.”"
"1620","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the call to prayer is called, Satan turns away from his horn so that he does not hear the call to prayer. Then, when the call is made, he accepts, until when he repents with prayer, he turns away. Until, when the tathwib is finished, it begins, until it comes between a person and himself, saying: Remember such-and-such, when he did not remember, until he continues A person does not know how much he has prayed.”"
"1621","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If people knew what is in the call, and the first row, and then they had no choice but to throw arrows for it, they would have done so, even if they knew what is in the displacement, They would have raced to it, and if they had known what was in the dark and the morning, they would have come to them, even if they had crawled.”"
"1622","Abba Ahmad bin Suleiman, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Saeed al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Asi, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, make me the imam of my people. He said: “You are their imam, and follow the example of “The weakest of them, and appoint a muezzin who takes no reward for his call to prayer.”"
"1623","Narrated by Qutaibah bin Sa’id, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “ When you hear the call to prayer, say what the muezzin says.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1624","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muja’im, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, he said: I heard Muawiyah, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard the muezzin and said: “Like what he said.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1625","Anba Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Mujma’ bin Yahya Al-Ansari, who said: I was sitting with Abu Umamah bin Sahl, and he gave the call to prayer. The muezzin, and he said: “God is great, God is great,” so he said “Allahu Akbar” twice, and said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God,” so two people testified, so he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so he testified twice, then said: This is what Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan told me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1626","Anba Mujahid bin Musa and Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Amr bin Yahya told me that Jesus Ibn Omar told him, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Alqamah Ibn Waqqas, on the authority of Alqamah Ibn Waqqas, he said: I was with Muawiyah when his muezzin gave the call to prayer. So Muawiyah said as the muezzin said, until when he said: “Come to prayer,” he said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” Then when he said: “Come to prayer.” Al-Falah,” he said: “There is no power nor strength except in God,” and after that he said what the muezzin said, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And he said that"
"1627","Anba Muhammad bin Salamah said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, that Bukayr bin Al-Ashjaj narrated to him, that Ali bin Khalid Al-Du’ali He told him that an-Nadr ibn Sufyan al-Du’ali told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood up. Bilal called out, and when he remained silent, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says the like of what he said with certainty will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1628","Suwaid bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: Ka’b bin Alqamah told me, that he heard Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, the client of Nafi’ bin Amr al-Qurashi, narrates that he heard Abdullah bin Amr say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “When you hear the muezzin, say what he says, then pray for me, for whoever prays a blessing upon me, may God bless him ten times, then pray for me.” I have the means, for it is a status in Paradise, which is not appropriate except for one of the servants of God. I hope that I am he, so whoever asks for me? the means, intercession was granted to him.”"
"1629","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he hears the muezzin, ‘And I bear witness that there is no god but God’ Alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. I am satisfied with God as Lord, with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, as Messenger, and with Islam as religion. “His sin will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1630","Amr bin Mansour Abu Saeed Al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says when he hears the call: O God, Lord of this perfect supplication And the ongoing prayer, give Muhammad the means and the virtue, and raise him to a praiseworthy station which You promised him, intercession will be permitted for him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1631","Abu Qudamah Ubayd Allah bin Saeed Al-Sarkhasi reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Khams, who is Ibn Al-Hasan Al-Basri, trustworthy. He said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Between every two calls to prayer, between “Every two calls to prayer is a prayer, and between every two calls to prayer is a prayer, for whoever wishes.”"
"1632","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abu Amir reported, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Amir, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: “The muezzin was calling for the Maghrib prayer, and he would go to the door of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pillars, praying the two rak’ahs, until The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come out while they were praying.”"
"1633","Anba Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki, on the authority of Sufyan, said: Omar bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah, and a man passed through the mosque after the call until he interrupted it. Abu Hurairah said: “As for this man, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Peace be upon him” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1634","Anba Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim reported, he said: Ja`far ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Umays, he said: Abu Sakhrah reported, on the authority of Abu Ash Sha’atha’, he said: A man came out of the mosque after the call to prayer, and Abu Hurairah said: “As for this man, he has disobeyed Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1635","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib, Amr ibn al-Harith, and Yunus informed us, that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray while he finished his prayers.” The evening prayer until dawn is eleven rak'ahs. He says the salaam every two rak'ahs, then prays the Witr prayer with one rak'ah, and prostrates as many prostrations as he recites. One of you recites fifty verses before he raises his head. Then, when the muezzin of the dawn prayer is silent, and the dawn prayer becomes clear to him, he gets up and performs two rak’ahs. two light times, then he lay on his right side until the muezzin comes to him for the establishment, and he goes out with him.” And some of them add to others in the story Hadith"
"1636","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal. On the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, that Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, told him, saying: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace, at night? He described that “he prayed eleven rak’ahs reciting the Witr prayer, then he fell asleep until he rested, and I saw him blowing the wit.” Then Bilal came to him and said: Prayer, oh Messenger of God, “So he stood up, prayed two rak’ahs, and prayed for the people, but he did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1637","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the prayer is established, do not get up until you see me come out.”"
"1638","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala, Kufi, told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God mislead those before us from the Friday prayer. So the Jews had Saturday, and the Christians had Sunday, so God brought us and guided us to Friday, so God made Friday. And Saturday, and Sunday, and likewise they will follow us on the Day of Resurrection, and we are the last of the people of the world, and the first on the Day of Resurrection. “The One who judges them before creation.”"
"1639","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram Al-Nasa’i told us, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We are the last, the first on the Day of Resurrection. We are the first people to enter Paradise, however Indeed, they were given the Scripture before us, and We gave it after them, so God guided us to the truth regarding what they differed about. This is the day on which they differed. In it, the people belong to us in it, tomorrow for the Jews, and for the Christians the day after.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1640","Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We are the last, the forerunners, but they were given the Book before us. And We were given it after them, and this is the day which God had ordained for them, so they disagreed therein, so God guided us to it, meaning Friday, so the people We have followers therein, the Jews tomorrow, and the Christians the day after.”"
"1641","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us, he said: Al-Mu’afa told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “The first Friday prayer was gathered after the first Friday prayer was gathered with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, it was gathered in Jawitha in Bahrain. “A village belonging to Abd al-Qais.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1642","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Ubaida bin Sufyan al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Al-Ja`d al-Dhamri, and he had companions, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever abandons three congregational prayers out of neglect, God will mark his fate.” \His heart\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1643","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr Al-Sarhi Al-Misri told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Usayd bin Abi Usayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever neglects to pray Friday prayers for three days without necessity, God will set a seal on his heart.”"
"1644","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Basri told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Katheer told us, on the authority of Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq On the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Mina, that he heard Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar speaking, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, And he said, while he was on the pillars of his pulpit: “Some people will stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or their hearts will be sealed, and then they will be \Among the heedless ones\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1645","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told me, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zaid bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Mina, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas. Ali said: Then he wrote about it to me, on the authority of Ibn Umar and my father. Huraira said that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the pillars of his pulpit: “Some people will stop abandoning Friday prayers.” Or that their hearts will be sealed, and then they will be among the heedless.”"
"1646","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, he said: Mufaddal bin Fadalah told me, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abbas, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The spirits of Friday, “It is obligatory for every pubescent person.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1647","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qudama bin Wabarah, on the authority of Samurah. Ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever neglects the Friday prayer without an excuse, let him give in charity a dinar, and if he does not find it, then half.” \dinar\"""""""
"1648","Nasr bin Ali told us, Nuh told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever neglects the Friday prayer intentionally, he owes a dinar, but if he does not find it, then half a dinar. And in another situation, he does not owe it intentionally. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1649","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, and he told us Harun bin Musa, who said: Abu Damra told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: Abd al-Rahman al-Araj told me that he heard Abu Kitten, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best day on which the sun rose is Friday, on which Adam was created, and on which he entered Paradise, and therein I will be expelled from it.”"
"1650","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir Al-Sulami, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar Ziyad bin Kulayb, on the authority of Ibrahim On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Al-Qartha’ Al-Dhabi, who was one of the first reciters, on the authority of Salman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “There is no A man purifies himself on Friday as he was commanded, then leaves his house until Friday comes, then he listens until the imam finishes his prayer, unless As an expiation for what happened before that Friday.”"
